# Layout, 2026

Lay out for the window, not the device. Read size with `currentWindowAdaptiveInfoV2()` from `androidx.compose.material3.adaptive`, and pass that size class down as state. That call includes large and extra-large widths. Do not branch on phone, tablet, or orientation.

Width: compact under 600dp, medium under 840dp, expanded under 1200dp, large under 1600dp, extra-large from 1600dp. Check height too. A landscape phone is often medium width and compact height, and two panes do not fit there.

## What to build

Play requires Tier 3 in April 2027: fill the window, no letterboxing, and keep scroll, text, and playback across rotation, fold, and resize. Build to Tier 2.

The home screen follows `dev_notes/basic_layout.txt`. On compact and medium width, a tab row holds Today, Hourly, Extended, and Radar. Today is first and selected at launch; the other three follow the order set in Settings. On a tall, narrow window, Hourly and Extended may run vertically per the orientation setting. On expanded width, drop the tabs: stack the cards in the main column and put Radar in a supporting pane so the cards are not stretched across the window. Do not add a bottom navigation bar. There is one home, not a destination per card. Settings and the city panel open from the header.

## Do not

- Set `screenOrientation`, `setRequestedOrientation`, `resizeableActivity="false"`, `minAspectRatio`, or `maxAspectRatio`. Target 37 ignores those when the smaller side is at least 600dp.
- Use a fixed screen width, a stretched single column, or an `isTablet` check.
- Wrap the whole window in `safeDrawingPadding()`. Call `enableEdgeToEdge()`. Set `windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"`. Pad interactive content with `WindowInsets.safeDrawing`. Let backgrounds draw behind the system bars.
- Drop list selection or scroll position when the size class changes. Hoist that state.

Touch targets are at least 48dp. Text must survive a large font scale. A real screen gets previews at compact, medium, and expanded width.

Add the adaptive Compose artifact when the first real screen needs it, not before.
